=========================================================
ARCHITECTURE
============

```
         Azure Virtual Network
             (cloud-vnet)

     --------------------------------
     |                              |
     |                              |
  VM1                             VM2
```

Private IP                     Private IP
10.0.0.4                       10.0.0.5

VM1 and VM2 communicate securely using:

1. SSH
2. SCP
3. Private IP Addresses

=========================================================
STEP 5 : CONNECT TO VM1
=======================

Command:
chmod 400 vm1_key.pem

Purpose:
Provides secure permission to SSH private key.

Command:
ssh -i vm1_key.pem azureuser@VM1_PUBLIC_IP

Example:
ssh -i vm1_key.pem [azureuser@20.xx.xx.xx](mailto:azureuser@20.xx.xx.xx)

Purpose:
Connects securely to VM1.

=========================================================
STEP 6 : CONNECT TO VM2
=======================

Open another terminal.

Command:
chmod 400 vm2_key.pem

Command:
ssh -i vm2_key.pem azureuser@VM2_PUBLIC_IP

Purpose:
Connects securely to VM2.

=========================================================
STEP 7 : GET PRIVATE IP OF VM2
==============================

Inside VM2:

Command:
hostname -I

Example Output:
10.0.0.5

Purpose:
Gets private internal IP address of VM2.

=========================================================
STEP 8 : TEST COMMUNICATION
===========================

Inside VM1:

Command:
ping VM2_PRIVATE_IP

Example:
ping 10.0.0.5

Purpose:
Checks communication between both virtual machines.

Stop:
CTRL + C

=========================================================
STEP 9 : CREATE SAMPLE FILE IN VM1
==================================

Inside VM1:

Command:
nano sample.txt

Paste:

This file was transferred securely between Azure cloud instances.

Save:
CTRL + O
Enter
CTRL + X

Purpose:
Creates sample file for secure transfer.

=========================================================
STEP 10 : COPY VM2 KEY INTO VM1
===============================

Run this command from LOCAL MACHINE:

Command:
scp -i vm1_key.pem vm2_key.pem azureuser@VM1_PUBLIC_IP:/home/azureuser/

Example:
scp -i vm1_key.pem vm2_key.pem [azureuser@20.xx.xx.xx](mailto:azureuser@20.xx.xx.xx):/home/azureuser/

Purpose:
Copies VM2 SSH key into VM1 for authentication.

=========================================================
STEP 11 : GIVE PERMISSION TO VM2 KEY
====================================

Inside VM1:

Command:
chmod 400 vm2_key.pem

Purpose:
Provides secure permission to VM2 SSH key.

=========================================================
STEP 12 : TRANSFER FILE SECURELY
================================

Inside VM1:

Command:
scp -i vm2_key.pem sample.txt azureuser@VM2_PRIVATE_IP:/home/azureuser/

Example:
scp -i vm2_key.pem sample.txt azureuser@10.0.0.5:/home/azureuser/

Purpose:
Transfers file securely from VM1 to VM2 using SCP.

=========================================================
STEP 13 : VERIFY FILE IN VM2
============================

Inside VM2:

Command:
ls

Purpose:
Displays transferred files.

Command:
cat sample.txt

Purpose:
Displays file contents transferred from VM1.

=========================================================
STEP 14 : SET SECURE FILE PERMISSIONS
=====================================

Inside VM2:

Command:
chmod 600 sample.txt

Purpose:
Allows only owner to read and write file.

VERIFY:

Command:
ls -l

Expected Output:
-rw-------

=========================================================
IMPORTANT COMMANDS
==================

SSH Connection:
ssh -i key.pem azureuser@PUBLIC_IP

Get Private IP:
hostname -I

Check Communication:
ping PRIVATE_IP

Create File:
nano sample.txt

Transfer File:
scp -i key.pem sample.txt azureuser@PRIVATE_IP:/home/azureuser/

View Files:
ls

Read File:
cat sample.txt

Set Permissions:
chmod 600 sample.txt

=========================================================
IMPORTANT CONCEPTS
==================

SSH:
Secure protocol used for remote login.

SCP:
Secure Copy Protocol used for encrypted file transfer.

Virtual Network:
Private Azure network connecting cloud resources.

Private IP:
Internal IP used for communication between VMs.

chmod 600:
Restricts file access to owner only.

